        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the inconsistent handling of byte order for the GUID structure, where some fields were stored in little-endian format while others were in big-endian format. This discrepancy led to incorrect representations of GUIDs when they were converted to strings or parsed from text, violating the EFI specification. The use of a custom `efi_guid_t` structure instead of the standard `EFI_GUID` structure further complicated the situation, as it did not adhere to the expected byte order defined in the EFI specification.

